.Dd June 2026
.Dt DEPLOY-RB 1
.Os bfcodec 0.0.6
.Sh NAME
.Nm deploy-rb
.Nd build a REFLEC BEAT plus mulist and deploy it to an iOS device
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op options
.Ar HOST
.Ar APP-UUID
.Ar UUID
.Ar FILE ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
builds a complete
.Pa mulist
from a set of song packages and deploys it, together with the packages, to a jailbroken iOS device over SSH.
Only the Japanese release
.Pq Li jp.konami.rbplus
is supported as a target.
.Pp
When invoked as
.Nm deploy-jbt
.Pq normally an installed symbolic link, or a copy on Windows ,
the package type defaults to
.Li jbt
instead of
.Li rb .
.Pp
Each input
.Ar FILE
is a BFCodec-encrypted ZIP archive
.Pq .rb or .jbt .
For
.Li rb
packages the
.Pa goodrb.json
database is the authority: every input is matched by its SHA-256, which also selects the single decryption key, and unmatched or undecryptable files are skipped.
The matched database id, not the input filename, names the file written to the device.
Packages the database marks as bundled ship inside the app and are skipped unless
.Fl -process-bundled
is given.
.Pp
World-version
.Pq Li jp.konami.rbplusw
packages cannot be read by the supported app.
They are skipped unless
.Fl -convert-world
is given, which re-encrypts them from the world key to the Japanese DLC key.
When a world package and its Japanese equivalent are both supplied, the Japanese copy is preferred.
.Pp
The plaintext mulist has four random bytes prepended and is then encrypted with the key derived from the device
.Ar UUID
.Pq the MD5 of its canonical uppercase form
before being copied to the device.
.Ar UUID
and
.Ar APP-UUID
must be valid UUIDs; dashes are optional.
.Ar APP-UUID
names the per-application container directory under
.Pa /var/mobile/Containers/Data/Application
on the device.
.Pp
.Ar HOST
is the SSH host.
It may be a bare hostname or IP address, or a URI of the form
.Ql [user[:password]@]host[:port]
that also sets the user, password, and port.
Values parsed from the URI take precedence over the
.Fl -user
and
.Fl -port
options.
A password is fed to
.Xr ssh 1
and
.Xr scp 1
through
.Xr sshpass 1 ,
which must be installed; it cannot be combined with
.Fl -rsync .
.Pp
The mulist is always copied with
.Xr scp 1 .
The song packages also use
.Xr scp 1
unless
.Fl -rsync
is given and the device has
.Xr rsync 1 ,
in which case rsync is used; rsync requires public-key authentication.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-N, --process-non-matching"
.It Fl W , Fl -convert-world
Re-encrypt world-version packages for the Japanese release instead of skipping them.
.It Fl -db Ar path
Path to the
.Pa goodrb.json
.Pq or Pa goodjbt.json
database used to validate packages by SHA-256.
By default the database is read from the installed
.Pa share/bfcodec
directory, located relative to the executable.
On a standalone Windows build the current directory is tried first, then
.Pa share/bfcodec
beside the executable.
On Linux and macOS the current directory is never used.
.It Fl d , Fl -debug
Enable debug-level logging.
.It Fl y , Fl -dry-run
Simulate every step, creating no files and only logging commands.
.It Fl i Ar file , Fl -identity Ar file
SSH identity
.Pq private key
file.
.It Fl j Ar n , Fl -jobs Ar n
Number of files to process in parallel.
Default is the number of CPUs.
.It Fl K , Fl -keep
Keep the staging directory after deployment instead of removing it.
.It Fl p Ar password , Fl -password Ar password
SSH password, fed to
.Xr ssh 1
and
.Xr scp 1
through
.Xr sshpass 1 .
Overridden by a password given in
.Ar HOST ;
incompatible with
.Fl -rsync .
.It Fl P Ar port , Fl -port Ar port
SSH port.
Default is 22.
Overridden by a port given in
.Ar HOST .
.It Fl B , Fl -process-bundled
Include packages the database marks as bundled, which are skipped by default.
.It Fl N , Fl -process-non-matching
Process every input file without consulting the database.
This disables the SHA-256 check.
.It Fl r , Fl -rsync
Use
.Xr rsync 1
for the song packages when the device has it.
Requires public-key authentication; the mulist itself is always copied with
.Xr scp 1 .
.It Fl S Ar dir , Fl -staging-dir Ar dir
Local directory for the built mulist and renamed packages.
When given it must already exist and be writable.
Otherwise a uniquely named
.Pa .deploy-rb-*
directory is created in the current directory, or in the system temporary directory when the current directory is not writable.
.It Fl t Ar type , Fl -type Ar type
Package type selecting the decryption keys:
.Li rb
or
.Li jbt .
Default is
.Li rb .
.It Fl u Ar user , Fl -user Ar user
SSH user.
Default is
.Li mobile .
Overridden by a user given in
.Ar HOST .
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Report each step.
.It Fl -help
Print a help message and exit.
.It Fl -version
Print version and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "SSHPASS"
.It Ev SSHPASS
When a password is supplied, it is exported here for
.Xr sshpass 1
so that it never appears on a command line.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
A non-zero status is also returned when any input package was skipped.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jbt 1 ,
.Xr unjbt 1 ,
.Xr rsync 1 ,
.Xr scp 1 ,
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr sshpass 1
